      "verifiedVia": "Validated by criterion-3 against INDEPENDENT pySecDec, which builds the Symanzik U/F directly from the graph and never reads the anc reduction or its 32 masters. crit-1 (clean planar pole) and crit-2 (Euclidean reality) do not apply to a non-planar four-point (genuine u-channel cut; no all-spacelike region); their role is taken by the removability argument and by Minkowski crit-3. crit-3: at five Minkowski points {(7,-2),(7,-3),(11,-2)} (s-channel physical) and {(-9,2),(-9,4)} (u-channel physical, s13>0), all orders eps^-3..0, the stored series matches the contour-deformed (+i0) pySecDec oracle in both real and imaginary parts to Monte-Carlo accuracy: every cell is within ~2 sigma of the pySecDec error (tolerance 8 sigma), and the opposite branch is rejected by 1e3 to 1e7 sigma. At the s-channel points the principal-branch evaluation equals pySecDec directly; at the u-channel points it equals the complex conjugate, the expected real-analytic (Schwarz) reflection f(s+i0)=conj(f(s-i0)). The validation content is the branch-free real-part agreement (<=1.3 sigma at all 20 cells), the imaginary-part magnitude match, and the correct direct-versus-conjugate sign at each point, since any real-analytic symbol in {s,t,-u} satisfies the conjugation pattern; a wrong reconstruction would still pass the conjugation but fail the value match (a flipped crossed-master sign shifts the eps^0 coefficient by ~1e4 sigma). A fresh independent i2m reduction reproduces the stored series exactly. The two new crossed masters Ax1234{2} and Fx12{35} contribute above the Monte-Carlo band at every order, and their separate contribution vectors across the five points and four orders are linearly independent (rank 2), so crit-3 constrains each of them individually. STVerify's automatic Euclidean verification point is not applicable to this non-planar entry (no all-spacelike region; STVerify returns 'no Euclidean kinematic point found'); the Euclidean pySecDec that backs STVeri